<title>SOUTH AFRICA: GUNDLE H1 SHR RISES, PROSPECTS SEEN GOOD.</title>
<headline>GUNDLE H1 SHR RISES, PROSPECTS SEEN GOOD.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-05-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Half year ended March 31 </p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)	 </p>
<p>    Shr, (cts)		18.3	  vs  13.8</p>
<p>    Attrib income	   2.69	  vs  2.02</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		   3.07	  vs  2.32</p>
<p>    Tax			 0.38	  vs  0.29</p>
<p>    Net financing costs   0.92	  vs  0.81</p>
<p>    Turnover		  51.8	  vs  40.11</p>
<p>Full name: Gundle Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE - The company said no dividend had been declared.</p>
<p>It said that subject to stable labour relations and no major</p>
<p>deterioration in the economy, the company should continue to</p>
<p>perform well.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
